original_row.English:
If a house fell upon him and upon his wife:
the heirs of the husband say: “The wife died first and afterwards the husband died”;
the heirs of the wife say: “The husband died first and afterwards the wife died”—
the House of Shammai say:
Let them split it;
But the House of Hillel say:
The property remains in its prior possession:
the marriage settlement remains in the possession of the heirs of the husband;
property that comes in and goes out with her remains in the possession
of the heirs of the [wife’s] father.114

